  "summary": "On January 11, 2026 monitoring software at Langley Twigg Law in Napier, New Zealand flagged unauthorized activity, and the firm disconnected its network and later restored systems from backups. The Anubis ransomware gang claimed the attack on January 25 and published stolen files, including internal operational information and client documents copied from the firm's file server and reportedly passport scans, followed by further releases and the full 380 GB dataset. The firm obtained a High Court injunction on February 5 against accessing or distributing the data and notified the Privacy Commissioner and police.",
